.SH NAME
CWE\-303 \- Incorrect Implementation of Authentication Algorithm
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The requirements for the product dictate the use of an established authentication algorithm, but the implementation of the algorithm is incorrect. This incorrect implementation may allow authentication to be bypassed.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB2\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2023\-29357
Microsoft SharePoint Server, added 2024\-01\-10, ransomware: Known.
.PP
Microsoft SharePoint Server Privilege Escalation Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Microsoft SharePoint Server contains an unspecified vulnerability that allows an unauthenticated attacker, who has gained access to spoofed JWT authentication tokens, to use them for executing a network attack. This attack bypasses authentication, enabling the attacker to gain administrator privileges.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply mitigations per vendor instructions, or discontinue use.
 Due 2024\-01\-31.
.PP
